{# Shared by the /, /home, /communities/@x and /collaborate feeds: the
   pre-paint column restore. Included from the top of each page's
   {% block content %} so the feeds cannot drift apart.

   It sits in the body rather than the head because the nav is boosted, and a
   boosted response has its entire <head> thrown away bar the title — left up
   there it would simply stop running the moment anyone reached a feed through
   the nav, and the grid would ignore their saved column count. At the top of
   the content it still runs before the grid below it is parsed, so it is
   still applied before that grid paints, and htmx re-executes it on every
   boosted swap.

   No page-width override lives here any more. It used to widen the whole page
   to 1600px, which moved the header too — the logo and nav sat flush left on
   these three pages and centred everywhere else. The grid section opts into
   .center-wide instead, so only the grid is wide. #}
{# Applied before first paint so the grid does not flash at another width. #}
<script>
  (function () {
    var saved = parseInt(localStorage.getItem("homeCols"), 10);
    if (saved > 0) {
      document.documentElement.style.setProperty("--home-cols", saved);
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-cols", "");
    }
  })();
</script>
